  "decision": "Comment Issued",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Sufficient evidence has been submitted to demonstrate, on the balance of probabilities, that the property known as Flat 20, Chequer Court, 3 Chequer Street, London, EC1Y 8PW has been in continuous use as a self-contained residential unit (Use Class C3) for a period exceeding four years prior to the date of this application.\nThe submitted documentation, including council tax records, utility bills, TV licensing information, and planning history, is considered sufficiently precise and unambiguous. There is no evidence available to the Local Planning Authority to contradict or otherwise undermine the applicant’s version of events.\nAccordingly, the use of the property as a single dwellinghouse is considered to be lawful and immune from enforcement action under Section 171B of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended)."
  ],
